As the tides change, the water level in a bay varies sinusoidally. At high tide today at 8 A.M., the water level was 15 feet; at low tide, 6 hours later at 2 P.M., it was 3 feet. How fast, in feet per hour, was the water level dropping at noon today? (A) 3 (B) π\sqrt{3}/2 (C) 3\sqrt{3} (D) π\sqrt{3}

Answer:

